		(property "Note" "REPLACES THE OBSOLETE ICS-43434 (FBV2-S1-006). Not a pin-compatible swap: the DMM-4026-B-I2S-R has SEVEN pads and a different land pattern, so both the symbol and the footprint are new. Verified against the PUI Audio data sheet Rev A, 5/26/2021. Pin 1 LR to GND selects the LEFT I2S slot. Pin 2 CONFIG has no ICS-43434 equivalent and MUST be tied to GND - the data sheet says Pull to ground, the state of this pin is used at power-up. Pin 3 VDD 1.62 to 3.63 V with C8 100 nF local. Pin 4 GND is the ring pad around the acoustic port. Pin 7 SD tri-states off-slot, and the data sheet requires a 100 kOhm pull-down on the SD trace - that is R120. CLOCK CONSTRAINT: normal mode needs BCLK between 2.048 and 4.096 MHz, so a 16 kHz / 64-BCLK frame (1.024 MHz) would NOT keep this microphone in normal mode. Run the shared I2S bus at 48 kHz with a 64-BCLK frame - 3.072 MHz, the data sheet typical - and decimate to 16 kHz in firmware. Below 320 kHz the part drops to sleep mode at 5 uA. Startup 20 ms. Supply current 820 to 1000 uA. BOTTOM PORT: acoustic port 0.25 mm diameter in the can; the PCB needs a 1.05 mm hole concentric with pad 4, and the enclosure tunnel must align to it."
			(at 116.84 81.28 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
